      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "MIGHTY CRUNCH (6) has been a bit hot and cold and that continued last start when he finished second, beaten 5 metres, in a nice return to form at this track over 1850m. May need luck at some stage extracting from the inside of the second row. His recent form is good enough to put him right in the finish. KINGSBURY (5) was beaten narrowly two runs ago then went close again last time over 1780m at Redcliffe, finishing second and just a head from the winner. Good enough to win a race of this calibre. MOVE HEAVENNEARTH (3) is in the mix at her first run since finishing fourth over 1780m at Redcliffe ten weeks ago. WEE BONNIE (8) is worth plenty of thought off a last-start win by 4.5 metres at Redcliffe over 1780m when leading all of the way as the warm favourite.",
